From edec216117d563c244ebedd2e565fa286b9ab94b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Dapp <robin.dapp@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:18:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] RISC-V: Error out early for unsupported builtins. [PR127553]

Right now we only show an error if the expansion of a builtin fails.
But there is builtin code that get optimized away before expansion and
never shows an error message.  It's not strictly wrong code but at least
surprising and will mislead compilation checks.

This patch just copies the checks of expand_builtin to
check_builtin_call.  We don't have the exact same expression of the
affected call available at that point, though.  The basic fndecl just
contains the function name and not its arguments.  We can reconstruct
the call but in my tests there were always slight difference to the
expand-time diagnostic.  Therefore I adjusted the test expectations
instead.

	PR target/127553

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* config/riscv/riscv-vector-builtins.cc (validate_instance_type_required_extensions):
	Add location param for logging.
	(expand_builtin): Pass location.
	(check_builtin_call): Likewise.

